{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 50, :comments ["<b>Before the year of famine came.</b> We say in tractate Ta'anit: from here it is forbidden to have relations with one's wife in a year of famine. And the difficulty arises: how could Levi have had relations, since Jocheved was born between the walls, and at that time it was a year of famine, as it is written: כי זה שנתים הרעב? And Rabbi Yehudah the Hasid said: what is forbidden to have relations with one's wife applies for example to a prophet who heard from the mouth of the Holy One, blessed be He, that a famine is destined to come — such as Joseph, who knew the matter clearly by means of Pharaoh's dream; but Levi, who did not know the matter clearly, was not forbidden. And some explain that Levi and Joseph disagree in the dispute of the Tannaim who disagree in tractate Yevamot: for there are those who say there that the commandment of פריה ורביה is two males, and there are those who say he has not fulfilled it until he fathers a male and a female. And Levi held like the one who says until he also fathers a female, and therefore he had relations, since a female had not yet been born to him — and we say in tractate Ta'anit: those who have no children may have relations with their wives in a year of famine, in order to fulfill the commandment of פריה ורביה. And Joseph held like the one who says two males, and therefore he did not wish to have relations, since he had already fulfilled it."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:58.652842126Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}